# Project structure (WebApp)

Keep code in the folder that matches its role. Root: `src/WebApp/`.

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| **Endpoints/** | Minimal APIs and HTTP route handlers (`*Endpoints.cs`). Register groups in `EndpointExtensions.MapAppEndpoints`. |
| **Components/** | Blazor UI (pages, layout, shared). See `blazor-conventions.mdc`. |
| **Data/** | Blazor-facing backend: `Features`, `Persistence`, EF `AppDbContext`. |
| **AI/** | App AI behavior: MAF agents, workflows, tools, memory, and orchestration (C#). `_Legacy_Python/` is reference only. |
| **Models/** | DTOs, entities, constants. |
| **Utilities/** | Cross-cutting helpers (auth, DB setup, extensions). |

## Endpoints

- One file per area: `AuthEndpoints.cs`, `ChatEndpoints.cs`, etc.
- Namespace: `WebApp.Endpoints`
- Each file exposes `MapXxxEndpoints(this WebApplication app)`
- Wire new groups in `Endpoints/EndpointExtensions.cs` → `MapAppEndpoints`

Do not put minimal API routes under `Components/` or `Data/`.

## AI boundaries

- **Agents/**: LLM runners only. One class per agent role, named clearly, e.g. `IntentClassificationAgent`, `GeneralChatAgent`. Agents may build messages and call `AgentFactory`.
- **Agents/AgentProfiles.cs**: Keep agent profile keys, deployment names, names, descriptions, and instructions in C#. Do not put prompts/profile definitions in `appsettings`.
- **Tools/**: Plain C# capabilities exposed to agents via MAF tools. Tools may call app services/DB/APIs, but must not call LLMs or route chat turns.
- **Workflows/**: Multi-step MAF workflows that compose agents and tools. Keep placeholder `.gitkeep` files in empty workflow folders.
- **Orchestration/**: Turn-level coordination only: load memory, classify intent, route to an agent/workflow, return the result.
- **Utilities/Helpers/AzureAiFoundryHelpers.cs**: Keep Azure AI Foundry plumbing here: endpoint normalization, Foundry agent factory, and AI DI registration.
- **Models/DTOs.cs**: Keep small AI/config request/result/intent DTOs in the `# AI` region instead of an `AI/Contracts` folder.
- Do not add a `Skills/` folder unless a future capability layer has a clear responsibility distinct from agents and workflows.

## Foundry auth

- Use key-based Azure OpenAI configuration for now: `Foundry:Enabled`, `Foundry:Endpoint`, and `Foundry:ApiKey`.
- Put keys in user secrets or host environment variables (never commit keys).
